+# 20261018-123
+
+## Purpose and changes
+
+Directly translate the already-closed current-authority CSV/image deletion ownership unit: explicit kind/id/path command, Backend current-target calculation and shared reference-only detach, full validation/retry/one commit, actual reconciliation maps and commit-gated public work. Route selected deletion read through the official Backend query; adapt its existing legacy-import cleanup caller to the explicit reference shape. Cases110/111 plus case11 canonical path cover the bounded contracts. Code90 lineage/fingerprint and review042/Plan023 record pending exact-SHA Actions. Also record unit39 final exact-SHA109+109/repeat/build/cumulative/fidelity and the earlier incomplete split repeat honestly in review041.
+
+## Rationale and rejected alternatives
+
+Keep Source45/pseudocode23 authoritative; do not rewrite Source to permit the legacy caller candidate or reset an entire image slot. Reuse unit39 cascade/index mapping rather than invent a second delete-specific reference classifier. Reject blanket graph/asset selection clearing because reconciliation must preserve unrelated references. Do not accept id-only targets or reinterpret a mismatched kind. Retain existing aggregate rendering without falsely claiming supplied-state completion. Fingerprint from staged Git blobs is metadata calculation only, not an executed checker pass.
+
+## Scope, evidence and follow-up
+
+No policy, Source, pseudocode, optional model/TLC, generated dist or ownership hierarchy changes. Legacy import cleanup payload is compatible with the new Backend boundary; its larger rollback/import lifecycle remains unaligned and explicitly outside this unit. Unit39 source proof is ecce1fb4d8a45fda442984c1acd97196e403ecaa, not this later result document. Unit40 Actions111+111/repeat/build/version/fidelity pending; code stale and whole assets/move/import/schema/serializer/raster/dashboard/timing work remains. No local runtime/test/build/checker. Patch records actual modified files together with this explanation; no preparatory runtime bridge or duplicate state added.
